      "content": "I see. Looking at the data from a policy perspective, there's often a discussion about whether these shifts correlate with a measurable drop in social capital or \"civic trust.\" In many case studies, when these traditionally homogenous areas become more diverse, there's a reported sense of alienation among the original population. From a sociological standpoint, would it be accurate to say that this influx can fundamentally destabilize the underlying social infrastructure that these suburbs rely on to function effectively?",
